                        "form_id": "b7e8b88f-cbc6-4ab9-9c27-0c7025ddb7db",
                        "entry_id": "64f0a440-e6d5-39a1-86cc-97144c7020ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "слабоу́миях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a88c7450-a27c-33a6-86c3-59b4ace22ad4",
                        "entry_id": "64f0a440-e6d5-39a1-86cc-97144c7020ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "психиатр. стойкое оскудение и упрощение психической деятельности, характеризующееся нарушением познавательных процессов, поведения, обеднением эмоций и индивидуальных черт характера"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d327900-4d98-41e9-89a9-ef1e723a856e",
                                "sense_id": "a88c7450-a27c-33a6-86c3-59b4ace22ad4",
                                "text": "В Шалинском дурдоме не держали агрессивных опасных психов. Специализацией лечебницы было, наверное, простое слабоумие. В дурдоме жили невинные дурачки, с разной степенью недоразвитости ума."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "40287f54-7ed9-305b-8093-28e56eb62752",
                        "entry_id": "64f0a440-e6d5-39a1-86cc-97144c7020ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. идиотизм, глупость"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "530c7875-d622-45fe-8720-5641668bc78c",
                                "sense_id": "40287f54-7ed9-305b-8093-28e56eb62752",
                                "text": "Люди буквально падают от напряжения, ликвидируют все остатки разгильдяйства и слабоумия, люди, можно сказать, заикаются от напряжения."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3f51094-140d-4cb1-b27d-75e2dfb8f64e",
                        "source_entry_id": "64f0a440-e6d5-39a1-86cc-97144c7020ba",
                        "target_lang_word": "dementia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dementia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "076a5735-11b4-3409-8ded-8455a63c0d4b",
                                        "entry_id": "25ad1da9-36b9-3b10-b29c-258226ebbda3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A progressive decline in cognitive function due to damage or disease in the brain beyond what might be expected from normal aging. Areas particularly affected include memory, attention, judgement, language and problem solving."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd0140ad-2205-444f-be1b-69971a80b744",
                                                "sense_id": "076a5735-11b4-3409-8ded-8455a63c0d4b",
                                                "text": "Similar studies of rats have employed four different intracranial resorbable, slow sustained release systems— […]. Such a slow-release device containing angiogenic factors could be placed on the pia mater covering the cerebral cortex and tested in persons with senile dementia in long term studies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2788fef5-b4e9-479c-9e1d-921287e3d61a",
                                                "sense_id": "076a5735-11b4-3409-8ded-8455a63c0d4b",
                                                "text": "In recent years some clinical trials involving potential dementia drugs have had disappointing setbacks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7473f8e-1737-36d3-b03f-0f33753e0846",
                                        "entry_id": "25ad1da9-36b9-3b10-b29c-258226ebbda3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Madness or insanity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
